# Code style for this project

When writing code in this repository:

- Prefer functional React components
- Keep components modular and readable
- Use Tailwind utilities consistently
- Reuse existing patterns before creating new ones
- Keep class naming and layout structure clean
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction for simple UI sections
- For animations, respect the current GSAP / Locomotive architecture
- For icons, prefer the existing icon approach used in the repo (e.g. Lucide where already adopted)
- Avoid introducing new libraries unless clearly needed
- Check imports carefully and avoid broken dependency references
- Make sure code works with Vite
- Preserve responsive behavior across desktop, tablet, and mobile (see `responsive-mobile-first.mdc`)
